
## Dc database CSV changes, `5aafa2bf..HEAD`

**Scope:** six CSVs under `src/formats/dcdata/data/` changed. Of these, `DcList.generated.csv` and `formats.generated.csv` are generated artifacts — I verified they contain exactly the propagation of the source-table changes below, with no orphan edits. In the hand-edited tables, **`categories/el.csv` (26 changed rows) and 12 rows of `semantic.csv` are pure `@ident(...)` additions** — confirmed by programmatically normalizing away the idents and diffing every column. Everything else is listed below.

### 1. Grammar relaxations in `categories/semantic.csv` — four edits making framed collections nullable

All four follow the same theme: permitting *empty* metadata/flag records so FinderInfo/ExtendedFinderInfo round-trips work when a file has zero flags or zero metadata fields. (`+` = one-or-more, `*` = zero-or-more, `?` = optional group.)

| Dc | Entity | Old syntax | New syntax | Effect |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 388 | Begin file flags description | `:~ (…) 389` | `:~ (…)? 389` | An empty flags collection (`388 389`) is now valid; previously the list/539/397/561 alternation was mandatory |
| 401 | Begin Mac OS file metadata description | `:~ [^402]+ 402` | `:~ [^402]* 402` | A Finder metadata record may contain no fields at all |
| 406 | Mac OS Finder flags | `… \| (388 [^389]+ 389)` | `… \| (388 [^389]* 389)` | The flags expressed as a 388-block alternative may be empty |
| 490 | Begin Mac OS extended Finder info description | `:~ [^491]+ 491` | `:~ [^491]* 491` | An extended Finder info (FXInfo) record may contain no fields |

Commits: 401 in `f34c6fa83 "data: Fix syntax for Apple metadata"`, 490 in `b23778ac1`, 388/406 in `9dfd1c209 "wip: Dc parser refactor, continued"`. Note 388/406 already carried `@ident` at the base commit, so the `@ident` you see on 388's diff lines is pre-existing, not new.

### 2. New Dc entity in `categories/semantic.csv`

- **Dc 562 (`1114674`) — "Mac OS extended Finder flags"** — a brand-new semantic Dc, not an annotation:
  - Syntax: `:~ [number:Natural0] | (388 [^389]* 389)` — identical shape to Dc 406 (classic Finder flags)
  - Description: "Extended Mac OS Finder flags (FXInfo fdXFlags / DXInfo frXFlags)."
  - Added in `9dfd1c209`; used by `2e0979de9 "feat: Implement Generalized Struct Projection onto Flags (406 388, 562 388, 388)"`.
  - It has **no `@ident`** — deliberate per the AGENTS rule (named constants only when referenced in procedural code), but worth flagging since it distinguishes it from the ident-only rows.

### 3. Format ontology additions in `categories/formats/database.csv` — three non-ident directives

- **f410 CscJournal:** `@magic_name("Collective Toolbox csc journal")` added to an otherwise empty directive column.
- **f632 CscJournal4:** `@magic_name("Collective Toolbox csc journal, version 4")` appended to its existing `@implies`/`@based_on` set. Per `4f4c9b48e`'s message (CSV edits landed in `2b87e697b`), these make `CTBCSCJ` file-magic descriptions resolve to the exact format version instead of falling through to first-wins extension lookup.
- **f411 CscDesc:** `@implies(f0)` added — an entailment that csc description files are UTF-8 (`f0` = UTF-8). From `d333f9d3b "…CscDesc encoding entailment"`.

### 4. Named-type range narrowed in `README-named-types.csv`

- `format` syntax rule changed from `:[f0..f1114111]` to `:[f0..f632]`. The token range for format references is now capped at 632, the highest defined FormatId, instead of spanning the whole Dc space. From `e378fd1bc "wip: Continue Dc parser refactoring"`.

